WEBVTT

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.780
The festival of dreams
to crown the strongest Pokémon Trainer...

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.450
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.490
The eight mighty trainers
aiming for the summit...

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.700
...have begun battling.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:21.380
The third match of the first round
pit the Champion of Sinnoh, Shirona, against...

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.000
...the Champion of Isshu, Iris.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.840
Amid their fierce fight,
Shirona surprised everyone with Mega Evolution.

00:00:32.010 --> 00:00:36.020
Though Iris put up a brave fight,
she lost by a narrow margin.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.520
And the fourth match,
which is about to begin...

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.770
...is finally Satoshi’s turn to battle.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:24.830
Now, for the fourth match
of the first round!

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:31.090
The Champion of Hoenn, Competitor Daigo,
versus Alola’s first Champion, Competitor Satoshi!

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.420
This is it!
The brat boy, meow!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.470
Against some impressive
strong guy!

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:38.890
The brat boy’s
got no chance, does he?

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.890
Hop, can you scoot over a bit?

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:45.980
Okay!

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.020
The Champion of Isshu?!

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.320
Hey!

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:52.110
I hear you’re
Mr. Dande’s little brother!

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.190
Nice to meet you!

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.150
Nice to meet you...

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:58.160
Wooloo! You’re so fluffy!

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:00.540
But what are you doing
in the stands?

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.540
She said she wants to feel
the stadium’s excitement firsthand.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.870
Isn’t that what Satoshi said?

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:09.090
You may each use three Pokémon
in the first round.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.750
No limit on
switching out Pokémon.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.010
Whoever makes all three of their opponent’s Pokémon
unable to battle will be the winner.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:21.760
Additionally, you are allowed a single use of only one
of the following: Daimax, a Z-Move, or Mega Evolution.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.060
Satoshi has all of them!

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:24.930
Yeah!

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.890
All his adventures
have led to this!

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.940
Mr. Daigo!
<i>We’ll</i> be heading on to the semifinals!

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:35.490
You sound so confident
despite facing me.

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:38.490
I can’t wait to see
how this battle will go.

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:42.990
Now then, both battlers,
send your first Pokémon out onto the field!

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:43.790
Three!

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:44.790
Two!

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:45.790
One!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:46.620
Go!

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.170
Come out, Metagross!

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:49.670
Uonoragon, I choose you!

00:03:57.970 --> 00:04:00.970
Both sides have sent out
their Pokémon.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:04.970
Metagross and Uonoragon
will face off in the first clash.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:08.310
Let’s see what you’ve got, rookie!

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.270
Let the battle begin!

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.020
Water Gun!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:13.190
Agility!

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.450
Jaw Bite!

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.330
Psychokinesis!

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:24.580
All right!

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.710
Jaw Bite subdued
the Psychokinesis!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.590
So you predicted that.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.340
Good going, Satoshi.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.890
The power of Jaw Bite increases
if it goes first, too.

00:04:41.890 --> 00:04:44.560
Plus, its ability is Strong Jaw!

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.850
That makes it even stronger!

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.730
Shinji...
Our battle helped me out!

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:56.730
Approaching with Agility,
then using Psychokinesis...

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:02.370
That training really <i>was</i> meant to prepare me
for a battle with Mr. Daigo!

00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:05.580
Return, Metagross.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.330
Come out, Bossgodra!

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:16.590
Competitor Daigo
already swaps out his Pokémon!

00:05:17.130 --> 00:05:21.090
Bossgodra! Iron Armor Pokémon!
Steel/Rock type!

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:24.510
With a horn sharp enough
to perforate thick iron sheets,

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.600
it brings down its opponents
by ramming into them horn first!

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.600
Satoshi, did you know...

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:38.730
...that I’m the strongest and most impressive
trainer in the Hoenn Region right now?

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.860
But that’s not enough to satisfy me.

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.780
The Pokémon World Championships...

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:51.120
By winning this tournament, I’ll be able to call myself
the one true strongest and most impressive trainer!

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.250
I’ve never seen him
this passionate before.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.300
Same goes for us!

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:03.010
For everyone who cheered us on,
all the way here...

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.050
...and for the Pokémon, too!

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.520
I’ve gotta win this!

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:11.350
Dragon Dive!

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:15.730
Heavy Bomber!

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.160
Can you keep going, Uonoragon?

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:40.250
Uonoragon is unable to battle!

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:43.260
Bossgodra gets the referee’s fan
in a clash of strength!

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:49.430
Uonoragon... lost...

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.390
Mr. Daigo’s strong...

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.020
See?

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:57.560
The brat boy just can’t cut it.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.190
What’s got into you?

00:06:59.190 --> 00:07:00.360
Are you... angry?

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:02.530
I am <i>not</i> angry!

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.240
Return, Uonoragon!

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:10.530
You really gave it your all.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.750
This time, Gänger...
I choose you!

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.720
Let’s do it!
Will-O-Wisp!

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.230
A Fire move...

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:46.740
Looks like Bossgodra can’t keep its strength up
due to the burn condition!

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.330
Smart Horn!

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:01.880
The burn condition
saps away its strength!

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.090
G-Gänger, here it comes!

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.800
Rock Seal!

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:11.180
Magical Shine!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:23.940
It’s still standing?!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.620
Bossgodra...

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:36.950
Bossgodra is unable to battle!

00:08:37.410 --> 00:08:39.870
All right!
You did it, Gänger!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:44.340
Even steel armor
couldn’t save it from a burn?!

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.430
That training did come in handy!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:53.180
Looking good,
Satoshi, Gänger!

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:56.600
That looked like
a pretty close win, though...

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.480
Return, Bossgodra!

00:09:00.390 --> 00:09:01.520
Thank you.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.820
Kudos to you.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.360
Come out, Yuradle!

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:13.370
Competitor Daigo’s
third Pokémon is Yuradle!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:17.370
Yuradle! Rock Crevice Pokémon!
Rock/Grass type!

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:23.540
Once it catches prey in its tentacles,
it digests them and absorbs their nutrients!

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:27.800
Power Whip!

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:37.260
Yuradle makes full use of its tentacles
with Power Whip!

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:39.270
Gänger has nowhere to run!

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.650
<i>It got caught!</i>

00:09:45.650 --> 00:09:48.150
So this is why he chose Yuradle?!

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:49.650
S-Scary...

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:50.990
Take Root!

00:09:58.660 --> 00:10:01.000
Take Root will stop him
from switching...

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:05.290
It’s a message,
saying he’ll take down Gänger here and now.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.050
Break free! Sludge Bomb!

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:22.940
It’s recovering!

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:27.980
But that means all his attacks will do is make Gänger more exhausted...

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:29.940
What’ll you do, Satoshi?

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:34.700
Meteor Beam!

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:47.330
That’s it!
Fight light with light!

00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.840
Gänger! Use Magical Shine!

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:20.370
That’s it!
Fight light with light!

00:11:20.780 --> 00:11:22.870
Gänger! Use Magical Shine!

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:56.450
Competitor Satoshi took advantage of
the colliding moves to carve Gänger an escape route!

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.320
Not bad.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.620
Move in! Shadow Ball!

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:04.540
Power Whip!

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.130
Gänger!

00:12:18.720 --> 00:12:21.220
Gänger is unable to battle!

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:24.810
Competitor Satoshi
has lost his second Pokémon!

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:29.520
Return, Gänger!

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.110
I won’t let your hard work
go to waste!

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:35.360
Pikachu, I’m counting on you!

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:41.410
There he is!
The flaming bolt of lightning, Pikachu!

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:43.530
Your greatest partner arrives.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:46.040
Pikachu! Go for it!

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:48.870
Electric moves
aren’t very effective.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.790
And he still has Metagross
to worry about.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:53.420
This is looking tense.

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:54.960
Pikachu’s out, meow!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.340
Can he turn it around?!

00:12:56.340 --> 00:13:00.380
Pikachu! If you don’t win this,
it’s all over, you hear?!

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:03.350
Rock Blast!

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:06.140
Lightning Speed!

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:16.190
Use the rocks to get a big jump!

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.620
So high...

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:25.660
But what’s he going to do?

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:29.660
The recovery won’t stop.
He has to end this quickly...

00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.500
Power Whip!

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:36.250
Electroweb!

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:40.260
What?!

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:41.630
All right! He got him!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:43.390
That was his plan?!

00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:45.640
Yeah! That’s what Satoshi does!

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:48.720
Now that’s good.
Intriguing!

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:54.020
Iron Tail!

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:11.460
Yuradle is unable to battle!

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:12.870
All right!

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:17.380
Daigo has lost
his second Pokémon.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.880
Now both sides
are down to their last!

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:24.470
Marvelous! Each and every one
of your attacks surprises me!

00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:27.430
Couldn’t do it without
Gänger setting up for Pikachu!

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:32.060
Oh, he’s so strong!
That’s our Pikachu!

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:33.890
This is the real thing, meow!

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:38.480
It’s looking like maybe
he just might...!

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:41.860
Return, Yuradle!

00:14:44.030 --> 00:14:45.780
You did well.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.580
Win or lose,
this will decide it all.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:49.990
Come out, Metagross!

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.620
Metagross...

00:14:56.630 --> 00:15:00.800
Now... For the fourth match
of the first round...

00:15:00.800 --> 00:15:04.130
Which of them
will advance to the semifinals?!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.680
Sparkle of stone...

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:08.930
Become our bond!

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:14.390
Metagross...

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:16.440
Mega Evolve!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:35.460
Competitor Daigo sends
Mega Metagross into battle!

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:38.080
Pikachu, use 100,000 Volts!

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:41.800
It’s pointless.

00:15:44.300 --> 00:15:46.800
Pikachu! Fire 100,000 Volts
again and again!

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:53.430
Pikachu can’t land a single hit!

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:59.310
Mega Metagross is accurately predicting
the trajectory of the lightning!

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:03.820
This is Mega Metagross!

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:06.820
It’s predicting every movement
Pikachu makes.

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:10.490
Comet Punch!

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:19.370
Pikachu!

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:32.760
Mega Metagross is said to have superior
strategic and information processing capabilities.

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.680
Every movement and breath
Pikachu takes...

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:38.890
It’s calculating them all instantaneously
and evading with ease.

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:42.190
You have a tough battle
ahead of you, Satoshi.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.120
Iron Tail!

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.290
Psychokinesis!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:06.000
Pikachu!

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:26.940
An overwhelming attack
by Mega Metagross!

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:29.740
Damage is piling up on Pikachu!

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:35.530
Competitor Daigo does not disappoint...
He’s coolly driving Competitor Satoshi into a corner!

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:43.130
Pikachu!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.590
Let’s use our full power!

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:50.510
What’s that?

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:51.590
A Z-Move!

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:54.050
Yeah! He finally used it!

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.100
A Z-Move, huh?

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:59.100
A Z-Move...

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.740
Far greater than 100,000 Volts...
1,000,000 Volts!

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:22.960
No, way, <i>way</i> greater than that!
Our super full power!

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:29.460
Pikachu! 10,000,000 Volts!

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:42.770
Metagross! Dodge it!

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:46.770
Luster Cannon!

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:49.980
What?!

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:50.780
All right!

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:59.910
He’s commanding
the electricity?!

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.750
Let’s finish this!
Iron Tail!

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:22.020
Metagross is unable to battle!

00:19:22.020 --> 00:19:28.190
Pikachu wins!
As such, the winner is Competitor Satoshi!

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.280
We did it!

00:19:35.780 --> 00:19:37.610
Competitor Satoshi wins!

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:42.660
Taking down the Champion of Hoenn, Competitor Daigo,
he advances to the semifinals!

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.790
He’s facing
Competitor Shirona next!

00:19:46.210 --> 00:19:48.670
So you made it, Satoshi.

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:51.500
He won! He won! He won!

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.670
What an electrifying 10,000,000 Volts!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:57.550
Pikachu, and the others under
Satoshi’s guidance, were incredible!

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:00.760
Today, we’re having a Galar special,
a curry party!

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.390
Yay!

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:04.810
Now there’s our Pikachu!

00:20:04.810 --> 00:20:06.560
There’s our brat boy!

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:09.190
Now, isn’t <i>this</i> quite the upset?!

00:20:09.190 --> 00:20:12.320
You know, maybe
they just might...!

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:17.780
Mr. Daigo.

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:21.450
The feelings you have
for your Pokémon partners…

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:25.830
And the feelings of those Pokémon,
responding to yours with all their might…

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:31.290
They came together as one,
and created an even greater power.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.960
And thus, you were able
to grasp victory today.

00:20:35.340 --> 00:20:37.170
A marvelous victory.

00:20:39.510 --> 00:20:45.640
With this, the four trainers advancing to the
Masters Tournament semifinals have been decided.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:51.810
Competitor Dande, Competitor Carne,
Competitor Shirona, and Competitor Satoshi.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:56.990
The white-hot Masters Tournament
is far from over!

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:02.990
You’re facing Ms. Shirona next.

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:07.000
But I’m sure
you and Pikachu can win.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.410
I believe in you.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:10.290
Satoshi, you better win!

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.460
I’ll be waiting to hear you’ve won!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.460
Yeah! Leave it to me!

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:17.800
You can’t let your guard down.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:20.180
I know that!

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:22.800
I’m <i>gonna</i> battle Mr. Dande,
for sure!

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.180
Right, Pikachu?

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:28.770
Best wishes!
Give it your all!

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:33.230
The fierce first round
of the Masters Tournament has concluded.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:37.570
Next is Dande versus Carne,
and Shirona versus Satoshi.

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:41.280
Now, which of these trainers
will win their way into the finals?!

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:07.240
Bari-bari...

00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:08.490
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:10.080
Kikuna here!

00:23:08.830 --> 00:23:15.350
I’ve got my plans for when I grow up in my pocket

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:12.500
Koharu and Eevee...

00:23:12.500 --> 00:23:15.330
From their mysterious encounter
at school, up until now...

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:18.420
They’ve really tried their hand
at lots of things.

00:23:16.780 --> 00:23:21.590
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:20.670
Break it down for me, Bari-chan...

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:23.300
Koharu and the Eevee
that doesn’t evolve...

00:23:21.590 --> 00:23:25.720
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:25.720
What do you think they’ll do next?

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:26.720
Mm-hmm...

00:23:25.720 --> 00:23:27.340
Let’s have a fight!

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:28.600
Ooh, ooh!

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:29.950
1. Once the battle’s done

00:23:28.600 --> 00:23:31.770
